---
import Feature from "../../layouts/Feature.astro"
import Beat from "../../components/Beat.astro"
import Term from "../../components/Term.astro"

const faq = [
  {
    q: "Can an AI agent write the config sync file?",
    a: 'Yes. Give your agent the <a href="/schemas/config-sync.json">config sync schema</a>, or have it run <code>pb config sync schema</code>: every key and example, exact.',
  },
  {
    q: "Which repositories work?",
    a: "Any Git repository you can reach: GitHub, GitLab, your own server or a local path, over HTTPS or SSH. It stays yours.",
  },
  {
    q: "Which files are never synced?",
    a: 'Credentials, <code>.env</code> files, SSH keys and Paperboat\'s own state are always left out. Keep secrets in <a href="/features/env/">ENV</a>.',
  },
  {
    q: "What if a file differs between macOS and Linux?",
    a: "Give each operating system its own path in the sync file, or give one machine its own rule. Paperboat never guesses a path.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can a team share defaults?",
    a: "Yes. A team sets a default repository, and each member chooses per machine whether to follow it.",
  },
]
---

<Feature
  slug="config-sync"
  title="Sync dotfiles across machines | Paperboat"
  description="Keep the same dotfiles and settings on every machine, from a Git repository you own. You approve every change."
  headline="The same setup on every machine"
  faq={faq}
  related={["env", "recipes", "terminal"]}
>
  <p slot="lede">Your shell, editor and tool settings, the same on every machine. They come from a Git repository you own, and nothing changes until you say so.</p>
  <Term slot="aside" lines={["$ pb config repository connect \\", "    git@github.com:ana/dotfiles.git", "$ pb config sync apply", "~/.zshrc            update", "~/.config/nvim/     add", "# review the changes, then confirm"]} />

  <Beat id="approve-title" title="You approve every change">
    <p>See what will change on a machine before it does. Nothing is overwritten behind your back.</p>
    <Term slot="visual" lines={["$ pb config status", "studio    in sync", "gpu-box   1 change waiting", "laptop    1 conflict"]} />
  </Beat>

  <Beat id="conflict-title" title="Conflicts, side by side" flip>
    <p>When a file changed on the machine and in the repository, compare the two and keep the one you want.</p>
    <Term slot="visual" lines={["$ pb config conflict compare laptop .zshrc", "$ pb config conflict resolve laptop .zshrc \\", "    --keep repository"]} />
  </Beat>

  <section class="section section-rule" aria-labelledby="details-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="visually-hidden" id="details-title">Details</h2>
      <div class="points points-3">
        <div>
          <h3 class="h3">Your repository</h3>
          <p>Plain files in Git, with their history, wherever you keep your code.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="h3">Per system, per machine</h3>
          <p>One path on macOS, another on Linux, and one machine that does its own thing.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="h3">Secrets left out</h3>
          <p>Keys, credentials and .env files are never synced, whatever the rules say.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Feature>
